(footprint "SW_Push_1P1T_XKB_TS-1187A"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "SILK OUTLINE CORRECTED 2026-07-29: the four side verticals were drawn from each corner inward to y=+/-1.05 at x=+/-2.55, which runs them straight THROUGH the pads (pad x 2.00..3.60, pad y 1.15..2.35) — kicad-cli DRC silk_over_copper x4. The break was cut on the wrong axis. They now exist only in the pad-free band |y| <= 1.05. SPST-NO momentary tact switch, XKB TS-1187A-B-A-B (C318884), SMD-4P gull-wing, 5.1 x 5.1 x 1.5 mm. DECLARED-PARTIAL LAND: XKB publishes no datasheet PDF and no recommended land for this SKU (LCSC C318884 re-read 2026-07-28), so the pads are deliberately oversized to 1.60 x 1.20 at (+/-2.80, +/-1.75) to tolerate +/-0.4 mm of lead-position error; jlc_twin PAD-GEOM at stage 7 is the gate that closes it. Pads 1-2 are one contact, 3-4 the other (standard 4-pad tact arrangement, asserted not quoted) - benign here because 1/2 carry USB_BOOT and 3/4 carry GND, so any wrong pairing fails LOUDLY at first power-up.")
	(tags "tact switch SPST momentary SMD-4P XKB TS-1187A C318884 bootsel")
